<section class="wp-block-group alignfull has-accent-5-background-color has-background" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--70);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--70)"><!-- wp:heading {"level":1} -->
<h1 class="wp-block-heading">Plan changes, domains and refunds</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"fontSize":"large"} -->
<p class="has-large-font-size">How WopCart plans handle upgrades, downgrades, domains and the EU right of withdrawal, in plain language.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"textColor":"accent-4","fontSize":"small"} -->
<p class="has-accent-4-color has-text-color has-small-font-size">This summary does not replace our Terms of Service and is not legal advice. If the two differ, the Terms apply.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">In short</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Upgrades</strong> take effect immediately. The prorated difference is charged at once.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Downgrades</strong> take effect at your next renewal. You keep your current plan until then.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Plan changes are <strong>not refunded or credited</strong>.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local and staging sites do not use a domain slot, up to 3 per key by default.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>You can withdraw from a plan purchase within 14 days for a full refund. Your plan key is then revoked and your sites return to the free plan.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"backgroundColor":"accent-5","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull has-accent-5-background-color has-background" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Upgrading</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you move to a plan with more domains, the change takes effect immediately, and we charge the prorated difference for the rest of your current billing period at once.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Example: you move from Single (€89 per year) to Studio (€179 per year) halfway through your year. The yearly difference is €90, so about €45 is charged when you upgrade. The exact amount depends on the days remaining.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Downgrading</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When you move to a plan with fewer domains, the change takes effect at your next renewal. Until then, you keep the plan you paid for. From the renewal, you are billed the lower price.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If more domains are active than the new plan allows, you choose which sites stay. If you do not choose, the oldest activations are kept. You can withdraw a scheduled downgrade before the renewal date.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"backgroundColor":"accent-5","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull has-accent-5-background-color has-background" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">No refunds or credits for plan changes</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Plan changes never result in a refund or account credit. An upgrade charges only the difference for the remaining period, and a downgrade waits until the period you already paid for has ended.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">When a plan ends</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After a paid plan ends, the store returns to the free plan. Every feature keeps working, and payments are routed through WopCart's Stripe Connect platform with the 2% fee instead of your own gateway accounts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"backgroundColor":"accent-5","layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull has-accent-5-background-color has-background" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Domains and staging sites</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Each production domain where the plan key is saved uses one domain slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local and staging sites do not use a slot. By default, up to 3 of them can be active on one key at the same time.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Local sites include <code>localhost</code>, private IP addresses and addresses ending in <code>.local</code> or <code>.test</code>. Staging sites include subdomains such as <code>staging.</code>, <code>dev.</code> or <code>test.</code> and common hosting staging domains.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>You can remove a domain in your wopcart.com account to free its slot and use the key on another site.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Removing the plan key from a site's settings also releases that site's slot.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>If wopcart.com cannot be reached, a site on a paid plan keeps its plan for up to 14 days.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:group {"tagName":"section","align":"full","style":{"spacing":{"padding":{"top":"var:preset|spacing|60","bottom":"var:preset|spacing|60"}}},"layout":{"type":"constrained"}} -->
<section class="wp-block-group alignfull" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">14-day right of withdrawal</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Every customer can withdraw from the purchase of a paid plan within 14 days, without giving a reason. This applies to consumers and businesses, and even after you have received and activated your plan key.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To withdraw, email info@wopcart.com with your order number. We refund the full amount within 14 days to the payment method you used. At the same time, we revoke your plan key, and all sites that use it return to the free plan. Your sites and store data are not affected. After the 14 days, paid plans are not refunded.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This does not affect your statutory rights, for example if the product is faulty or not as described.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></section>
<!-- /wp:group -->

